					on the <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>: Starter free forever, Pro at $39 USD
					per tenant per month covering unlimited installs.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="alt-faq-q">
				<h3>Why would I stay on iRedMail?</h3>
				<p>
					You need OS-native install (no Docker).
					You run BSD. You need OpenLDAP as a backend.
					Your team has deep iRedMail muscle memory and the modern surface isn't worth
					retraining for. If none of those apply, Vectis Mail's API, declarative config,
					and orchestrated updates are a clear step up.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
